# Accountix — Persian (fa) message catalog.
#
# Two source languages feed this catalog (ADR-045/046). Template,
# form and view strings are written in Persian, so their msgids ARE
# Persian and their msgstrs stay EMPTY on purpose — gettext falls
# back to the msgid itself, which is exactly the Persian text to
# render. Service messages and model choice labels are written in
# English in the source; since Sprint 21 (ADR-047 — Jason's product
# decision) those English msgids carry real Persian msgstrs here,
# so the default UI renders them in Persian too. Without a compiled
# fa.mo those entries fall back to the English msgid (the
# pre-Sprint-21 behaviour), so compilemessages is required for fa
# as well as en. Real translations into other languages live in
# their own locales.
#
